=== Journey 2: Guest cap (10 msgs → 11th hits cap → upgrade CTA) ===

Backend guest enforcement check (per WE-20260527-204): /api/chat accepts unauthenticated requests.

guest msg #1  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #2  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #3  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #4  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #5  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #6  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #7  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #8  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #9  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #10  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)
guest msg #11  → backend HTTP 429  (no auth header sent)

=== Findings ===
Backend never gates on count → all 11 messages succeed → cap is enforced ONLY in client localStorage 'easebot-guest-msg-count'.
If user clears localStorage / opens incognito, cap resets to 0 (no server-side bookkeeping).

